/*
render3dxt.lcb - xTalk Builder (LCB) binding library for render3dxt, a
                 textured 3D software renderer, via the render3d_shim C shim.
                 Part of the xTalk Suite for OpenXTalk (OXT).

Once this extension is loaded, every public handler below is callable
directly from xTalk script, e.g.
    set the imageData of image "View" to r3SceneRender(sScene, 640, 480)

Conventions (the shim, src/render3d_shim.c, is where each is enforced; they
are box3dxt's, so the two libraries read alike):
  * Handles are integers (0 = invalid). Every handler tolerates a stale or 0
    handle: getters return 0 or empty, actions do nothing.
  * NAMES ARE MECHANICAL: the handler for the shim's r3x_node_set_position is
    r3NodeSetPosition; nothing is renamed by hand. tools/check-lcb-signatures.py
    holds the bijection (every export bound once, every binding wrapped by the
    one public handler of that name).
  * Distances are METRES, y is up, a rotation is a quaternion x y z w, and the
    camera is eye, target and vertical field of view in degrees: box3dxt's
    numbers, so a scene it simulates is drawn from them unchanged.
  * A colour is three numbers, 0 to 255.
  * A result of several numbers comes back as TEXT, comma-separated, with a
    "." decimal point in every locale. Text crosses as a Pointer that textOf()
    copies, never as ZStringNative (the engine frees a returned C string).
  * Text going IN crosses as ZStringUTF8; bytes going in (a picture file, an
    imageData) as the Data's own byte pointer and length.
  * The picture comes OUT as a Data built from the shim's frame buffer by the
    engine's MCDataCreateWithBytes: one copy, one call across the boundary
    for a whole frame.
  * A yes/no crosses the public boundary as a Boolean and the C boundary as
    an int (asInt() below; `tR is not 0` on the way back).
  * Nothing here throws, bar the ABI check: a refused call returns 0 or empty
    and r3LastError() says why. A render call in a frame loop must not be
    able to stop the loop.

The foreign handlers bind to the shared library "render3dxt" (built by
CMakeLists.txt). Bindings resolve on first use.

The module is org.openxtalk.library.renderthreed, not ...render3dxt:
lc-compile warns on a digit in a namespace component and the Extension
Builder runs it with -Werror (box3dxt's gotcha 1).
*/

/**
A textured 3D renderer that draws into an image.

A scene holds nodes, lights and a camera. A node is a mesh (a box, a sphere,
a model loaded from an OBJ file) placed at a position with a rotation and a
size; a material gives it a colour, a texture and a shine. <r3SceneRender>
draws the scene and returns the picture, ready to be the imageData of an
image, so a stack shows 3D with one line in a frame loop. All the drawing is
done inside the library: thousands of textured triangles take a few
milliseconds.

Scenes, nodes, meshes, materials, textures and lights are integer handles.
0 means a call was refused or found nothing, and a stale handle is harmless:
getters return 0 or empty, actions do nothing. <r3LastError> says why a call
was refused.

Every distance is in metres with y pointing up, a rotation is a quaternion
(four numbers x, y, z, w) and a colour is three numbers from 0 to 255. A
result of several numbers comes back as comma-separated text such as
"1.5,0,-2", so item 1 of it is x.

The library is made to draw what box3dxt simulates. Positions, rotations
and the camera are the same numbers in both: give each node the body it
draws with <r3NodeSetTag>, and after every physics step hand box3dxt's
b3MovesText() to <r3SceneApplyMoves>.

Tags: Graphics, 3D, Library
*/
library org.openxtalk.library.renderthreed

use com.livecode.foreign

-- The engine's own builders, resolved by NAME (so no leading underscore).
-- MCStringCreateWithBytes: textOf() below. MCDataGetBytePtr and
-- MCDataGetLength: the read-only bytes of a Data handed in (coinxt's proven
-- way; a Data's length is the engine's uindex_t, hence CUInt).
-- MCDataCreateWithBytes: the picture, copied out of the shim's frame buffer.
foreign handler MCStringCreateWithBytes(in pBytes as Pointer, in pByteCount as CUInt, in pEncoding as CUInt, in pIsExternalRep as CBool, out rString as String) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"
foreign handler MCDataGetBytePtr(in pData as Data) returns Pointer binds to "<builtin>"
foreign handler MCDataGetLength(in pData as Data) returns CUInt binds to "<builtin>"
foreign handler MCDataCreateWithBytes(in pBytes as Pointer, in pCount as CUInt, out rData as Data) returns CBool binds to "<builtin>"

metadata title is "render3dxt: 3D Renderer for OpenXTalk"
metadata author is "Seth Morrow Software"
metadata version is "0.1.0"
metadata summary is "A textured 3D renderer that draws into an image: models (OBJ), textures, lights, a camera, picking. Draws what box3dxt simulates."

